      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1907, educator Marietta Johnson opened Fairhope's School for Organic Education, later praised by John Dewey in his 1915 book Schools of Tomorrow.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairhope%2C_Alabama",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Fairhope became a winter haven for artists and intellectuals, drawing names like Upton Sinclair, Wharton Esherick, and Clarence Darrow.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
